# The ordinary-component branch of plane uniqueness

The built common reduction supplies the original 15.2.20 involution and
odd-core conclusions, and selects an actual escaping ordinary component
with its normal Sylow orbit and faithful marked action. Original15.2.23
now feeds this extraction directly. The marked A₆ and A₇ rows, PSL₃(3)
and large PSL₂(p) are excluded on these original groups. The nine non-J₄
sporadic rows are now excluded through their actual two-central quotient
actions, retaining the central two-covers. The small PSL₂ aliases are
transported into the characteristic-two rows by genuine isomorphisms.
The binary PSL₃, PSL₄ and PSL₅ rows and the three small-derived rows
Sp₄(2)′, G₂(2)′ and Tits are now excluded on that same component.
The general-field G₂, symplectic, triality and Ree rows, including the G₂(4)
central two-covers, are excluded by the original rank-two K in a marked
centralizer or solvable Sylow intersection. The Bender and nonbinary PSL₃
rows, including the permitted PSL₃(4) covers, are excluded by the literal
maximal intersection and concrete Borel fixer theorems. This constructs
the terminal model/action conclusion on the selected component.

Only J₄ remains. Its literal fixed-subgroup two-residual gives a genuine
triple-Mathieu section inside Kc. The original 15.2.12 alternatives make Kc
solvable or give it abelian Sylow three-subgroups; central transfer excludes
that section. `PlaneUniquenessPreceding.source_15_2_15` now proves the exact
singleton statement under the explicit earlier source packet, HStar wreath
quotients, Kc orbit and structural alternatives, restricted action and plane
inverter. Construction of those earlier inputs remains with the existing
geometry/small-parabolic producers and final chosen-action assembly.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith, 15.2.20 and 15.2.24, refs/quasithin.pdf.
-/
